{{ 'pm-homepage.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  pm-family-data is rendered, not included — some shops reject
  the include tag outright ("Include usage is not allowed in this
  context"). {% render %} runs in an isolated scope, so it can't
  assign into this template directly; capture its text output instead
  and split it here.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture pm_families_raw -%}{% render 'pm-family-data' %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign pm_families = pm_families_raw | strip | split: ';;' -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Every bag is one Shopify product with a Color option holding several
  variants, not separate per-color products — Shopify has no setting
  that renders one Product as multiple collection-grid tiles (Combined
  Listings runs the opposite direction: merging separate products into
  one PDP). So the grid below explodes each product into one tile per
  color itself. Pre-count how many tiles that actually produces, so the
  piece count and the "don't break mid-product" campaign-tile logic
  further down both use the real tile count instead of the product
  count.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign total_tile_count = 0 -%}
{%- for product in collection.products -%}
  {%- assign color_option = nil -%}
  {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
    {%- assign option_name_downcase = option.name | downcase -%}
    {%- if option_name_downcase == 'color' or option_name_downcase == 'colour' -%}
      {%- assign color_option = option -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if color_option -%}
    {%- assign total_tile_count = total_tile_count | plus: color_option.values.size -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign total_tile_count = total_tile_count | plus: 1 -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

<div class="pm-homepage">
  {%- comment -%}
    AW27 banner — coded directly here rather than as a separate section
    on an alternate template, so the AW27 collection can stay on the
    same default template every collection uses (no template selection
    or assignment step in Admin, and it can never end up pointed at the
    wrong collection). Gated on the handle so no other collection
    (Shop All included) picks up a banner it never asked for.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if collection.handle == 'aw27' -%}
    <section class="pm-hero">
      <a href="{{ section.settings.aw27_banner_link | default: '#' }}" class="pm-hero-media">
        {%- if section.settings.aw27_banner_image -%}
          <img src="{{ section.settings.aw27_banner_image | image_url: width: 1800 }}" alt="AW27" loading="eager">
        {%- else -%}
          <img src="{{ 'pm-drive-hero.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="AW27" loading="eager">
        {%- endif -%}
      </a>
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Category sub-nav — the reference (Gucci) shows a row of bag-type tabs
    under the main nav. Palera's site is organized by family/model line
    rather than bag type, so this reuses the same family list as the Shop
    mega-menu (pm-family-data) instead of inventing categories with no
    real collection behind them. Each tab is a real link to this same
    page with ?family=... — clicking one is a normal page navigation,
    not an in-place filter. There's no real per-family Shopify
    Collection to filter server-side (Shopify caches rendered HTML by
    URL, so query-string-driven server content isn't safe to rely on —
    a cached response could show one visitor a family meant for another),
    so the page that loads still sorts itself out client-side once on
    arrival (see data-family on each tile, and the script at the
    bottom) rather than as a live, click-driven filter.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <nav class="pm-plp-subnav" data-pm-family-nav>
    <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url | default: '/collections/all' }}" class="pm-plp-subnav-item is-active" data-family-filter="">View All</a>
    {%- for family in pm_families -%}
      {%- assign family_parts = family | split: '|' -%}
      {%- assign family_name = family_parts[0] -%}
      {%- assign family_handle = family_name | handle -%}
      <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url | default: '/collections/all' }}?family={{ family_handle }}" class="pm-plp-subnav-item" data-family-filter="{{ family_handle }}">{{ family_name }}</a>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </nav>

  <div class="pm-collection-bar">
    <a href="{{ section.settings.back_url | default: '/collections' }}" class="pm-collection-back">
      ← {{ section.settings.back_label }}
    </a>
    <div class="pm-collection-bar-right">
      <span class="pm-eyebrow" data-pm-piece-count>{{ total_tile_count }} {% if total_tile_count == 1 %}piece{% else %}pieces{% endif %}</span>
      {%- if collection.sort_options.size > 0 -%}
        {%- assign sort_by = collection.sort_by | default: collection.default_sort_by -%}
        <div class="pm-collection-sort">
          <label for="PmSortBy" class="pm-visually-hidden">{{ 'collections.sorting.title' | t }}</label>
          <select id="PmSortBy" class="pm-collection-sort-select" data-pm-sort>
            {%- for option in collection.sort_options -%}
              <option value="{{ option.value }}"{% if option.value == sort_by %} selected{% endif %}>{{ option.name }}</option>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </select>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="pm-collection-header">
    {%- if section.settings.line_label != blank -%}<span class="pm-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.line_label }} — Family</span>{%- endif -%}
    <h1 class="pm-serif pm-collection-name" data-pm-collection-title>{{ collection.title }}</h1>
    {%- if collection.description != blank -%}
      <p class="pm-serif pm-collection-note">{{ collection.description | strip_html }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="pm-collection-grid-wrap">
    {%- if collection.products.size == 0 -%}
      {%- if collection.handle == 'aw27' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Coded placeholder spots, not a text message — so the page
          never reads as broken/empty while the real AW27 products are
          getting added in Admin. The instant collection.products has
          anything in it, this branch stops running and the real grid
          below takes over automatically — nothing to swap by hand.
          Always exactly 12 tiles for a consistent grid; each one pulls
          a real photo from this section's "Placeholder photo" blocks
          (add up to 12, in order) and falls back to the plain
          placeholder for any spot left unset.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign placeholder_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'placeholder_spot' -%}
        <div class="pm-plp-grid">
          {%- for i in (1..12) -%}
            {%- assign spot_block = placeholder_blocks[forloop.index0] -%}
            <div class="pm-plp-tile" aria-hidden="true"{% if spot_block %} {{ spot_block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
              <div class="pm-plp-tile-image">
                {%- if spot_block.settings.image -%}
                  <img src="{{ spot_block.settings.image | image_url: width: 900 }}" alt="{{ spot_block.settings.image.alt | escape | default: spot_block.settings.label }}" loading="lazy">
                {%- else -%}
                  {% render 'pm-media-placeholder', label: 'Photo', hover: true %}
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
              <div class="pm-plp-tile-info">
                <span class="pm-plp-tile-name">{{ spot_block.settings.label | default: 'Coming soon' }}</span>
                <span class="pm-plp-tile-price">—</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- else -%}
        <p class="pm-collection-empty">{{ section.settings.empty_label }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Product tiles are uniform (name + price sit above a plain,
        contained product photo — no gradient caption overlay), one per
        color (see the pre-count above). A campaign placeholder tile
        (real imagery to be dropped in later) breaks the grid every 12
        tiles, always landing on a fresh row since 12 is a multiple of
        both the 2- and 4-column layouts — widening to a full-width
        banner every third break.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pm-plp-grid" data-pm-plp-grid>
        {%- comment -%}
          This section's blocks can be a mix of "Editorial break" and
          AW27's "Placeholder photo" blocks — filter to just the
          editorial breaks so the lookup below can't accidentally grab
          a placeholder_spot block's unrelated settings.

          Shop All, AW27, and every family (client-side-filtered) view
          all share this one section instance/block list, but each
          needs its own campaign-photo count — so every "Editorial
          break" block carries a "Show on" scope, and only blocks
          matching the current page's scope are ever picked here. AW27
          is a real separate collection, so its scope resolves
          server-side from collection.handle; family views are a
          client-side filter on this same Shop All page, so
          "family"-scoped blocks are rendered after the grid (hidden by
          default) and shown/positioned by the script at the bottom
          once a family filter is applied.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign editorial_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'editorial_break' -%}
        {%- assign current_scope = 'shop_all' -%}
        {%- if collection.handle == 'aw27' -%}{%- assign current_scope = 'aw27' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- assign scoped_break_index = -1 -%}
        {%- assign tile_index = 0 -%}
        {%- for product in collection.products -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            No real per-family Collection exists to filter against, so
            sort each product into one of the 9 real families by matching
            keywords (pm-family-data) against its title. Products that
            don't match any keyword still show under View All, just not
            under any family tab.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign tile_family = '' -%}
          {%- assign title_downcase = product.title | downcase -%}
          {%- for family in pm_families -%}
            {%- if tile_family == '' -%}
              {%- assign family_parts = family | split: '|' -%}
              {%- assign family_name = family_parts[0] -%}
              {%- assign family_keywords = family_parts[2] | split: ',' -%}
              {%- for keyword in family_keywords -%}
                {%- assign keyword_downcase = keyword | downcase -%}
                {%- if tile_family == '' and title_downcase contains keyword_downcase -%}
                  {%- assign tile_family = family_name | handle -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Each bag is one product with a Color option holding several
            variants — split it into one tile per color (see the
            pre-count comment above the piece-count computation).
            Products with no Color option just render their one tile,
            same as before.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign color_option = nil -%}
          {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
            {%- assign option_name_downcase = option.name | downcase -%}
            {%- if option_name_downcase == 'color' or option_name_downcase == 'colour' -%}
              {%- assign color_option = option -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- if color_option -%}
            {%- assign color_values = color_option.values -%}
            {%- assign color_option_key = 'option' | append: color_option.position -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- assign color_values = 'x' | split: ',' -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- for color_value in color_values -%}
            {%- assign tile_index = tile_index | plus: 1 -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              tile_name is the product title with any " — Color" suffix
              stripped — colors here are baked into the product's own
              title text in Shopify (e.g. "Maxi Roma — Black" is the
              literal title, not a variant), not appended by this
              template, so this has to split it back off rather than
              just not appending it. Each color still gets its own tile
              (data-family, image, price, and the ?variant= link all
              still come from that specific color's variant/product),
              the displayed name just doesn't spell the color out.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign tile_name = product.title | split: ' — ' | first -%}
            {%- if color_option -%}
              {%- assign tile_variant = product.variants | where: color_option_key, color_value | first -%}
              {%- assign tile_price_varies = false -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- assign tile_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
              {%- assign tile_price_varies = product.price_varies -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- assign tile_image = tile_variant.featured_image | default: product.featured_image -%}
            {%- assign tile_price = tile_variant.price | default: product.price -%}

            <a href="{{ product.url }}{% if tile_variant %}?variant={{ tile_variant.id }}{% endif %}" class="pm-plp-tile pm-reveal" data-family="{{ tile_family }}" style="transition-delay: {{ tile_index | modulo: 8 | times: 70 }}ms">
              <div class="pm-plp-tile-image">
                {%- if tile_image -%}
                  <img src="{{ tile_image | image_url: width: 900 }}" alt="{{ tile_image.alt | escape | default: tile_name }}" loading="lazy">
                {%- else -%}
                  {% render 'pm-media-placeholder', label: 'Photo', hover: true %}
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
              <div class="pm-plp-tile-info">
                <span class="pm-plp-tile-name">{{ tile_name }}</span>
                <span class="pm-plp-tile-price">
                  {%- if tile_price_varies -%}From {{ tile_price | money }}{%- else -%}{{ tile_price | money }}{%- endif -%}
                </span>
              </div>
            </a>
          {%- unless tile_index == total_tile_count -%}
            {%- assign campaign_check = tile_index | modulo: 12 -%}
            {%- if campaign_check == 0 -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                Editorial breaks pull from this section's "Editorial
                break" blocks scoped to the current page (see above),
                in order — these are the "handles" a merchant fills in
                via the theme editor for real campaign photos/video,
                one per break as the grid scrolls. A break only renders
                a tile when there's an actual matching-scope block
                behind it — once those run out, later break points are
                skipped entirely (no gray placeholder tile with nothing
                to select an image for), so there are never more photo
                slots visible than blocks the merchant has actually
                added for this page.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign scoped_break_index = scoped_break_index | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- assign editorial_block = nil -%}
              {%- assign scan_index = -1 -%}
              {%- for candidate_block in editorial_blocks -%}
                {%- if candidate_block.settings.show_on == current_scope -%}
                  {%- assign scan_index = scan_index | plus: 1 -%}
                  {%- if scan_index == scoped_break_index and editorial_block == nil -%}
                    {%- assign editorial_block = candidate_block -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- if editorial_block -%}
                {% render 'pm-campaign-tile', campaign_block: editorial_block, hidden: false %}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endunless -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- unless current_scope == 'aw27' -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Family-scoped campaign tiles: rendered here (hidden) so
            they exist in the DOM for every family, not baked into any
            one family's position — the script below shows/positions
            them once a ?family= filter is actually applied.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- for family_block in editorial_blocks -%}
            {%- if family_block.settings.show_on == 'family' -%}
              {% render 'pm-campaign-tile', campaign_block: family_block, hidden: true %}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endunless -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

<script src="{{ 'pm-homepage.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script>
  (function () {
    var select = document.getElementById('PmSortBy');
    if (select) {
      select.addEventListener('change', function () {
        var url = new URL(window.location.href);
        url.searchParams.set('sort_by', select.value);
        window.location.href = url.toString();
      });
    }

    var grid = document.querySelector('[data-pm-plp-grid]');
    var nav = document.querySelector('[data-pm-family-nav]');
    if (!grid || !nav) return;

    var countEl = document.querySelector('[data-pm-piece-count]');
    var titleEl = document.querySelector('[data-pm-collection-title]');
    var baseTitle = titleEl ? titleEl.textContent : '';

    var allTiles = Array.prototype.slice.call(grid.querySelectorAll('.pm-plp-tile'));
    var productTiles = allTiles.filter(function (el) { return !el.classList.contains('pm-plp-campaign-tile'); });
    var shopAllCampaignTiles = allTiles.filter(function (el) { return el.getAttribute('data-show-on') === 'shop_all'; });
    var familyCampaignTiles = allTiles.filter(function (el) { return el.getAttribute('data-show-on') === 'family'; });
    // Original (server-rendered) order, excluding the family-scoped
    // tiles — those are appended after everything else and start
    // hidden, so they're not part of the default View All order.
    var originalOrder = allTiles.filter(function (el) { return el.getAttribute('data-show-on') !== 'family'; });

    // A freestyle (shuffled) order per filter, so a family tab doesn't
    // show the same fixed sequence every time — only applied within a
    // family filter; View All keeps the section's real product order.
    function shuffled(list) {
      var copy = list.slice();
      for (var i = copy.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
        var j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
        var tmp = copy[i]; copy[i] = copy[j]; copy[j] = tmp;
      }
      return copy;
    }

    function applyFilter(familyHandle, familyLabel) {
      var isFiltered = !!familyHandle;
      shopAllCampaignTiles.forEach(function (tile) { tile.classList.toggle('pm-is-hidden', isFiltered); });
      familyCampaignTiles.forEach(function (tile) { tile.classList.toggle('pm-is-hidden', !isFiltered); });

      var visibleProducts, orderedAll;
      if (!isFiltered) {
        productTiles.forEach(function (tile) { tile.classList.remove('pm-is-hidden'); });
        visibleProducts = productTiles;
        orderedAll = originalOrder;
      } else {
        visibleProducts = shuffled(productTiles.filter(function (tile) { return tile.getAttribute('data-family') === familyHandle; }));
        productTiles.forEach(function (tile) { tile.classList.toggle('pm-is-hidden', tile.getAttribute('data-family') !== familyHandle); });
        orderedAll = visibleProducts.slice();
        // Intersperse the family-scoped campaign tiles evenly through
        // the shuffled product list rather than lumping them at the end.
        if (familyCampaignTiles.length) {
          var spacing = Math.max(1, Math.floor(orderedAll.length / (familyCampaignTiles.length + 1)));
          familyCampaignTiles.forEach(function (tile, i) {
            var pos = Math.min(spacing * (i + 1) + i, orderedAll.length);
            orderedAll.splice(pos, 0, tile);
          });
        }
      }
      orderedAll.forEach(function (tile) { grid.appendChild(tile); });

      nav.querySelectorAll('[data-family-filter]').forEach(function (link) {
        link.classList.toggle('is-active', link.getAttribute('data-family-filter') === familyHandle);
      });
      if (countEl) {
        countEl.textContent = visibleProducts.length + ' ' + (visibleProducts.length === 1 ? 'piece' : 'pieces');
      }
      if (titleEl) {
        titleEl.textContent = isFiltered ? familyLabel : baseTitle;
      }
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      Family links (here and in the mega-menu/mobile drawer) are real
      <a href> navigations to this same page with ?family=... — clicking
      one is a full page load, not an in-place filter swap, so it reads
      as going to that family's page. There's still no real per-family
      Shopify Collection behind it, so the arriving page still needs to
      sort itself out client-side once — that's all this does now: read
      the family off the URL on load and apply it, with no click
      handling or history.pushState left to fight the browser's own
      navigation.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    var initialFamily = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('family');
    if (initialFamily) {
      var initialLink = nav.querySelector('[data-family-filter="' + initialFamily + '"]');
      if (initialLink) applyFilter(initialFamily, initialLink.textContent.trim());
    }
  })();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PM: Collection grid",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "back_label", "label": "Back link label", "default": "All Families" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "back_url", "label": "Back link URL", "info": "Point this at your Shop by Family page (/collections)." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "line_label", "label": "Line label override" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "empty_label", "label": "Empty collection message", "default": "New pieces for this family are on the way." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "aw27_banner_image", "label": "AW27 banner image", "info": "Only shown on the AW27 collection page." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "aw27_banner_link", "label": "AW27 banner link" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "editorial_break",
      "name": "Editorial break",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "show_on",
          "label": "Show on",
          "options": [
            { "value": "shop_all", "label": "Shop All" },
            { "value": "family", "label": "Family pages (any family)" },
            { "value": "aw27", "label": "AW27" }
          ],
          "default": "shop_all"
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "orientation",
          "label": "Orientation",
          "options": [
            { "value": "horizontal", "label": "Horizontal" },
            { "value": "vertical", "label": "Vertical" }
          ],
          "default": "horizontal"
        },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "video_url", "label": "Video URL (.mp4)", "info": "Overrides the image when set." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "caption", "label": "Caption" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "placeholder_spot",
      "name": "Placeholder photo",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label", "default": "Coming soon" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
